# {{ name }}

A [Vendure](https://www.vendure.io/) store{{#if storefront}} with a [{{ storefront.frameworkName }}]({{ storefront.documentationUrl }}) storefront{{/if}}, created with `@vendure/create`.

## Develop

`vendure dev` needs Docker or Podman. It starts a local PostgreSQL and Redis, and then the server, the worker and the Dashboard:

```bash
{{ dev }}
```

The first run writes the initial database migration into `{{#if serverDir}}{{ serverDir }}/{{/if}}src/migrations` and seeds the data recorded in `{{#if serverDir}}{{ serverDir }}/{{/if}}.vendure/create.json`. Commit the migration.

- Dashboard: http://localhost:{{ serverPort }}/dashboard
- Shop API: http://localhost:{{ serverPort }}/shop-api
- Admin API: http://localhost:{{ serverPort }}/admin-api
{{#if storefront}}
- Storefront: http://localhost:{{ storefrontPort }}
{{/if}}

## Project structure

{{#if serverDir}}
- `{{ serverDir }}/src/vendure-config.ts`: the Vendure configuration, a Cloud Config.
- `{{ serverDir }}/src/migrations/`: the database migrations.
- `apps/storefront/`: the {{ storefront.frameworkName }} storefront.
{{else}}
- `src/vendure-config.ts`: the Vendure configuration, a Cloud Config.
- `src/migrations/`: the database migrations.
{{/if}}

## Scripts

- `{{ dev }}`: start the local development environment.
- `{{ build }}`: compile the project.
- `{{ typecheck }}`: check the types.

## Deploy

Deploy to Vendure Cloud with `vendure cloud deploy`. To run Vendure on your own infrastructure instead, see [Self-hosting]({{ selfHostingGuideUrl }}).
